  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'slow food' emerged in Italy in the 1980s as a reaction to the increasing popularity of fast food. The movement aimed to promote local, seasonal ingredients and traditional cooking methods, which were seen as being under threat from industrial agriculture and mass production. Proponents of slow food argued that the emphasis on speed and convenience had led to a loss of culinary skills and a decline in the quality of food.\n\nIn recent years, the slow food movement has gained momentum worldwide, with many restaurants and cafes adopting the principles of slow food. However, some critics have argued that the movement has become commercialized, with 'slow food' becoming just another marketing label for expensive, trendy cuisine.\n\nDespite these criticisms, the core values of the slow food movement remain relevant today. By prioritizing local ingredients and traditional cooking methods, we can not only improve the taste and nutritional value of our food but also support small-scale farmers and preserve cultural heritage.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What was the main reason for the emergence of the slow food movement in Italy?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To promote local, seasonal ingredients\", \"To encourage mass production of food\", \"To increase the popularity of fast food\", \"To preserve cultural heritage\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To promote local, seasonal ingredients\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is one of the negative consequences of the emphasis on speed and convenience in food production?\",\n      \"options\": [\"A decline in the quality of food\", \"An increase in the popularity of fast food\", \"A loss of culinary skills\", \"None of the above\"],\n      \"answer\": \"A loss of culinary skills\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"The word 'industrial' in the text is used to describe which aspect of agriculture?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Local, seasonal ingredients\", \"Traditional cooking methods\", \"Mass production of food\", \"Industrial agriculture\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Industrial agriculture\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"The author suggests that the slow food movement has become commercialized. What does this imply about its original purpose?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It was always a marketing label for expensive, trendy cuisine\", \"It is now more focused on preserving cultural heritage\", \"Its core values remain relevant today\", \"None of the above\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It was always a marketing label for expensive, trendy cuisine\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"The text implies that the slow food movement has which of the following benefits?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Only supports small-scale farmers\", \"Only preserves cultural heritage\", \"Supports small-scale farmers and improves the taste and nutritional value of our food\", \"None of the above\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Supports small-scale farmers and improves the taste and nutritional value of our food\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
